  "title": "Authorise the estimacion and invoice it as a CFDI",
  "desc": "Measure the period concepto by concepto, value it against the precios unitarios, amortise the anticipo and hold the fondo de garantia, get the residente de obra to authorise the estimacion and raise the CFDI against the authorised figure.",
  "longDesc": "An estimacion is not an invoice and the difference is the whole workflow. The estimacion is the measured, priced and authorised statement of the period; the CFDI is the fiscal document raised against it, and the tax authority will stamp a CFDI whose figures nobody authorised just as happily as one whose figures everybody agreed. That is how a contractor ends up holding a stamped invoice for an amount the client will not pay, with the correction living in a cancellation and a reissue rather than in a conversation. Authorised first and invoiced second, the two documents say the same number and the amortizacion del anticipo is visible on both.",
